Z||000010||Don Roger||08-22-2001||10:18 AM||||Please folks, stay on-topic:<P>I was looking for info on Porsche spyder style rebodies. i.e. 550, RSK, RS60, RS61.<P>If anyone would like to start a thread on other body styles, well go do it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Don in Canada||||reg||7
Z||000011||Songman||08-22-2001||07:03 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Don Roger:<BR><B>Please folks, stay on-topic:<P>I was looking for info on Porsche spyder style rebodies. i.e. 550, RSK, RS60, RS61.<P>If anyone would like to start a thread on other body styles, well go do it!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Don in Canada</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Don...<P>Everyone was staying on topic. Seems that the general thought was that you meant the upcoming Porsche Spider that is not even released yet. There is a kit out there for this uncoming body style..<P>And just so you'll know and expect it... topics grow from the original thoughts almost every time. When you have 3000+ people expressing their ideas this can't be helped. My advice is to just expect it and not let it get to you and you'll be a lot happier...<P>And as for your question... I have never seen any kits for the older type Porsche bodies. The problem is that the mid-engine design of the Fiero doesn't always go so well with the rear engine design of the Porsches. And there is no width overhang. When you pull the panels off, the car is just as wide as it was before.<P>Welcome to the forum...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
